course: dictionary
lesson: 3662
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word fishing is a good example. «Fishing line, hooks, released balloons and plastic drink rings can tangle animals or be eaten by them.» A fishing line is the string used to catch fish, so here fishing means catching fish.
explain: Fishing can also be a doing word used in an informal way. Someone who is fishing for compliments wants people to praise them, but does not ask straight out. They are hunting for praise, not holding a rod.
explain: Fishing can also mean searching with your hand. If someone is fishing in a bag for their keys, their hand is moving about inside, feeling for something. To choose the right meaning, swap each one into the sentence and see which one makes sense.
fact: Fishing means catching fish, as a hobby or as a job.
fact: «Fishing for compliments» means trying to get praise without asking for it directly.
fact: Fishing can also mean searching with your hand, as in «she was fishing in her bag for her keys».
fact: Words such as «fishing rod», «fishing boat», «fishing line» and «fishing net» are all about catching fish.
fact: Always wear a life jacket on boats, and be careful of hooks.
exercise: «Fishing line, hooks, released balloons and plastic drink rings can tangle animals or be eaten by them.» What is a fishing line? | *A string used to catch fish | A type of fish | A kind of boat | A net for birds
exercise: Maya says her friend keeps posting photos, fishing for compliments. What does fishing for compliments mean? | *Trying to get praise without asking for it directly | Searching a bag for something lost | Catching fish in a pond | Writing a long letter to a friend
exercise: Dad is fishing in his coat pocket for his keys. What does fishing mean here? | Throwing rubbish away | *Searching with his hand | Asking for praise | Catching fish in a river
test: Which sentence uses fishing to mean catching fish? | *They went fishing on the lake at dawn. | He was fishing for a kind word from his teacher. | Fishing is the name of her favourite song. | She was fishing in her bag for a pen.
test: In «The Mekong giant catfish is now very rare because of dams and fishing», what does fishing mean? | *Catching fish, as a job or a hobby | Searching with a hand | Making a fishing net | Asking for praise
exam: Which meaning of fishing fits best in «She kept fishing in her bag»? | Asking for praise | Catching fish | *Searching with the hand, feeling for something
